PDF.js 6.3.289 (pdfjs-dist on npm), Mozilla, Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE).
legacy/build/pdf.min.mjs and legacy/build/pdf.worker.min.mjs, unchanged apart from the .js extension
(so every static host serves them as JavaScript). The legacy build, because the modern one needs
JavaScript features only the newest browsers have (Map.getOrInsertComputed). Used by /viewer.js.
Also from the package, loaded only when a PDF needs them: wasm/ (JBIG2 and JPEG 2000 image decoders,
colour management; without them most scans draw blank), standard_fonts/, cmaps/, iccs/.
To update: npm pack pdfjs-dist@<version>, copy the same files and folders into vendor/pdfjs-<version>/,
and change PDFJS in scripts/lib/resources.mjs.
